Module lowwater "Low Water" {
  Description "The Dyers' Terrace: the Upper Cistern, the Dyers' Basin with an arch on its floor, the Sump, Mag Torrin's vat-yard, and the house of Abel Lusk, who taught the Lock-Rhyme to two generations of keepers.".


  Place dyers_walk "the Dyers' Walk" is room within ammerlin at 1, 2 outdoors.
  Place cistern_lip "the lip of the Upper Cistern" is room within ammerlin at 0, 2 outdoors.
  Place basin_edge "the edge of the Dyers' Basin" is room within ammerlin at 2, 2 outdoors.
  Place basin_floor "the floor of the Dyers' Basin" is room within ammerlin at 2, 3 outdoors.
  Place vat_yard "Mag Torrin's vat-yard" is room within ammerlin at 3, 2 outdoors.
  Place lusk_house "Abel Lusk's house" is building within ammerlin.
  Place lusk_room "Abel Lusk's kitchen" is room within lusk_house at 0, 0.

  Passage second_stair "the Stair, from Measures Terrace to the Dyers' Walk" is steps between measures_square and dyers_walk taking 15 minutes.
  Passage cistern_steps "the steps to the cistern" is steps between dyers_walk and cistern_lip.
  Passage basin_path "the path along the basins" is path between dyers_walk and basin_edge taking 3 minutes.
  Passage yard_gate "the vat-yard gate" is gate between basin_edge and vat_yard.
  Passage lusk_door "Abel Lusk's door" is door between dyers_walk and lusk_room.
  Passage basin_ladder "the iron ladder down the basin wall" is steps between basin_edge and basin_floor
    opening when level(dyers) <= 1 "An iron ladder goes down the inside of the basin wall and into the water. Below the third rung there is nothing to see but black dye-water.".

  // Three bodies of water, and the two gates between them. Water passes from the higher to the lower, a mark a
  // watch, until they stand level or the lower is full; it is never made and never lost, only moved.
  Kind basin. Entity upper: basin "the Upper Cistern". Entity dyers: basin "the Dyers' Basin". Entity sump: basin "the Sump".
  Measure level(basin). Measure brim(basin).
  Initially Set level(upper) to 4. Initially Set brim(upper) to 5.
  Initially Set level(dyers) to 3. Initially Set brim(dyers) to 3.
  Initially Set level(sump) to 2. Initially Set brim(sump) to 3.

  Thing upper_gate "the upper gate" at cistern_lip {
    State wound_down "The upper gate between the Cistern and the Dyers' Basin is wound down. The Cistern's post stands at {level(upper)}, the basin's at {level(dyers)}.".
    State wound_up "The upper gate is wound up; water goes through it from the Cistern into the Dyers' Basin. The Cistern's post stands at {level(upper)}, the basin's at {level(dyers)}.".
    Change open "Wind the upper gate up" from wound_down to wound_up.
    Change shut "Wind the upper gate down" from wound_up to wound_down.
  }
  Thing sump_gate "the sump gate" at basin_edge {
    State wound_down "The sump gate at the foot of the Dyers' Basin is wound down. The basin's gauge-post stands at {level(dyers)}, the Sump's at {level(sump)}.".
    State wound_up "The sump gate is wound up; the Dyers' Basin pours through it into the Sump. The basin's gauge-post stands at {level(dyers)}, the Sump's at {level(sump)}.".
    Change open "Wind the sump gate up" from wound_down to wound_up.
    Change shut "Wind the sump gate down" from wound_up to wound_down.
  }
  Thing overflow "the Sump's overflow" at basin_edge {
    State chained "On the Sump's far side, a sluice the size of a door is chained shut. A painted board: WARD DRAIN. BY TORRIN'S YARD. KEEP SHUT.".
    State unchained "The Sump's overflow stands open; the Sump runs out of it down the Ward drain, by way of Mag Torrin's yard. The Sump's post stands at {level(sump)}.".
    Change open "Unchain the Sump's overflow and open it" from chained to unchained.
    Change shut "Close the Sump's overflow" from unchained to chained.
  }
  Rule upper_flows when state(upper_gate, wound_up) and level(upper) > level(dyers) and level(dyers) < brim(dyers) {
    Decrease level(upper) by 1. Increase level(dyers) by 1. }
  Rule sump_flows when state(sump_gate, wound_up) and level(dyers) > level(sump) and level(sump) < brim(sump) {
    Decrease level(dyers) by 1. Increase level(sump) by 1. }
  Rule overflow_runs when state(overflow, unchained) and level(sump) > 0 {
    Decrease level(sump) by 1. Assert vatsDrowned(vat_yard). }
  Relation vatsDrowned(place).

  // The gauge-posts tell the truth, every one of them, all the time.
  Observe cistern_gauge at cistern_lip when true "The Upper Cistern is a long stone tank under the terrace wall, brimming from the Stair. Its gauge-post stands at {level(upper)}, of five marks.".
  Observe basin_gauge at basin_edge when true "The Dyers' Basin is a square stone pool three marks deep, its water black-blue from a hundred years of dye. Its gauge-post stands at {level(dyers)}, of three marks. Below it the Sump, a lower tank, stands at {level(sump)}, of three.".
  Observe basin_shape at basin_edge when level(dyers) >= 2 "Down through the dark water something pale stands on the basin floor: the top of an arch, too far down to make out.".
  Observe basin_shallow at basin_edge when level(dyers) == 1 "The basin is down to its last mark. An arch stands up out of the shallows on the floor, carved, grey, too old for the terrace it is in.".
  Observe basin_dry at basin_edge when level(dyers) == 0 "The Dyers' Basin is empty, its walls striped blue to the brim. On its floor stands an arch of grey stone, carved all over.".
  Observe floor_scene at basin_floor when true "The basin floor is slick with blue silt to the ankle. In the middle stands an arch of fine grey stone with nothing behind it but more floor, its face carved with a row of four mouths, each open wider than the last, and beside each a mark like a note of the Sounding's.".
  Observe floor_stones at basin_floor when at(weight_a, basin_floor) or at(weight_b, basin_floor) or at(weight_c, basin_floor) "Round the arch's foot lie blocks of the same grey stone, squared, each with a hole through it for a rope.".
  Observe floor_wet at basin_floor when level(dyers) == 1 "The water is ankle-deep and very cold.".

  Observe walk_scene at dyers_walk when true "The Dyers' Walk runs along the third terrace between the Stair and the basins, under lines of dyed wool hung out to dry, so that you walk through a long room of blue and madder and weld-yellow, dripping. The terrace wall below is striped with old dye-runs to the Ward.".
  Observe walk_rhyme at dyers_walk when hour(clock) == 9 and not drawnToday(vat_yard) "The third bell rings from the Sounding, and all along the Walk the dyers look up, as if it had called each of them by name.".
  // The dyers' own draw: at nine, the third bell, Mag Torrin takes a mark of the basin into her vats for the day's blue.
  // At six each morning the Office's man winds the Cistern into the basin until it is full, and the Cistern from the Stair.
  Relation drawnToday(place).
  Rule mag_draws when hour(clock) == 9 and not drawnToday(vat_yard) and level(dyers) >= 1 and not vatsDrowned(vat_yard) {
    Decrease level(dyers) by 1. Assert drawnToday(vat_yard). }
  Rule mag_draws_seen at basin_edge when hour(clock) == 9 and drawnToday(vat_yard) and not toldDraw(vat_yard)
    says "At the third bell a sluice in the yard wall grunts open and a mark of the basin goes off into Mag Torrin's vats in a blue rush." {
    Assert toldDraw(vat_yard). }
  Relation toldDraw(place).
  Rule morning_fill when hour(clock) == 6 and drawnToday(vat_yard) {
    Retract drawnToday(vat_yard). Retract toldDraw(vat_yard). Set level(dyers) to 3. Set level(upper) to 4. Set level(sump) to 2. Assert state(upper_gate, wound_down). }
  Rule morning_fill_dry when hour(clock) == 6 and not drawnToday(vat_yard) and level(dyers) < 3 and not filledToday(vat_yard) {
    Set level(dyers) to 3. Set level(upper) to 4. Set level(sump) to 2. Assert filledToday(vat_yard). Assert state(upper_gate, wound_down). }
  Rule fill_resets when hour(clock) == 7 and filledToday(vat_yard) { Retract filledToday(vat_yard). }
  Relation filledToday(place).
  // Bailing, by hand, a mark at a time.
  Action bail_basin(actor: group, site: place) "Bail the Dyers' Basin with the dyers' buckets" {
    Description "Two hours of buckets for a mark of water, tipped down the dyers' drain.".
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, basin_edge) and level(dyers) >= 1 and level(dyers) <= 2.
    Time 12.
    On success { Decrease level(dyers) by 1. }
    Result "It is two hours of filling a leather bucket from the ladder, handing it up, and tipping it down the dyers' drain, and at the end your arms are blue to the elbow and the basin is a mark lower.".
  }

  // The arch: four mouths and four notes, and the stones of its foot.
  Kind arch_rubbing "a rubbing of the Dyers' arch" is treasure worth 0 weighing 0 described "Charcoal on a dyer's cloth: four mouths, each wider than the last, a mark like a note beside each, and over them a line of Aenean letters.".
  Relation rubbed(entity).
  Thing arch "the grey arch" at basin_floor {
    State carved "The arch's face is carved with four mouths in a row, each open wider than the last, each with a note-mark beside it, under a line of letters you cannot read.".
    Tries looking.
  }
  Action rub_arch(actor: group, site: place) "Take a rubbing of the arch's face on a dyer's cloth" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, basin_floor) and not rubbed(arch).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert rubbed(arch). }
    Result "You wet a dyer's cloth, lay it over the carving, and work charcoal over it until the mouths and their marks and the line of letters come up black. It will have to be someone else who reads it.".
  }
  Item rubbing "the rubbing of the arch" is arch_rubbing at basin_floor hidden until arch_rubbed.
  Discovery arch_rubbed "A rubbing of the Dyers' arch lies on the basin floor, taken on a dyer's cloth.".
  Rule rubbing_made when rubbed(arch) and not knows(party, arch_rubbed) says "You fold the cloth with the charcoal inside." teaches arch_rubbed { }
  Discovery arch_mouths "The grey arch on the Dyers' Basin floor shows four mouths, from closed to wide open, each beside a mark like one of the Sounding's notes.".
  Rule arch_looked when tried(arch, looking) and not knows(party, arch_mouths)
    says "Four mouths, carved by someone who had looked hard at mouths: a mouth shut, a mouth a little open, a mouth open to speak, and a mouth wide as if to swallow. Beside each, the same small mark, set higher each time: like the notes in a hymnal, four of them, low to high." teaches arch_mouths { }
  Kind weight_stone "an Aenean weight-stone" is treasure worth 1 weighing 4 described "A squared block of grey stone, cold, heavier than it looks, with a hole through it for a rope.".
  Item weight_a "a weight-stone" is weight_stone at basin_floor.
  Item weight_b "a weight-stone" is weight_stone at basin_floor.
  Item weight_c "a weight-stone" is weight_stone at basin_floor.

  // Mag Torrin and her vats.
  Observe yard_scene at vat_yard when not vatsDrowned(vat_yard) "A yard of tall wooden vats, steaming, each a different blue. Lengths of wet wool hang in the air between the vats like slow banners. Everything, the cobbles, the cat, the woman with the paddle, is some shade of blue.".
  Observe yard_ruined at vat_yard when vatsDrowned(vat_yard) "The vat-yard is a pond. Grey Sump water stands a hand deep across the cobbles and has gone into every vat, and the blues have all gone the same dull colour, like a bruise. Wool lies in it in heaps.".
  Person mag "Mag Torrin" at vat_yard {
    Role "dyer and widow of the Dyers' Terrace". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns she. Manner acerbic.
  }
  Topic mag_basin with mag "Ask Mag Torrin about the Dyers' Basin" when true once {
    Says "'It's my water.' Mag does not stop stirring. 'Mine and four other yards', by right, a mark a day each between us, and I take mine at the third bell for the blue, because blue wants the morning. The Office's man fills it again at six.' She points the paddle at you. 'And there's a stone thing on the bottom nobody's seen in my lifetime and my mother's. Don't go getting ideas. You drain my basin and I've no blue tomorrow.'".
  }
  Topic mag_sump with mag "Ask Mag what happens if the Sump runs over" when true once {
    Says "'Then it comes down the Ward drain, and the Ward drain comes through my yard, because my grandfather was a fool and built where it was cheap.' She nods at the vats. 'Sump water's grey. One hand of it in a vat and the dye's dead, the whole season's dead. Twice in my life. The second time I had to sell my husband's boat.'".
  }
  Relation askedEarly(group).
  Topic mag_early with mag "Ask Mag to take her blue now instead of at the third bell" when not drawnToday(vat_yard) and hour(clock) >= 6 and hour(clock) < 9 and level(dyers) >= 1 and not vatsDrowned(vat_yard) once {
    Says "Mag looks at the sky, and at you, and at the basin. 'Early blue's thin,' she says. 'But I suppose thin's better than none, which is what I'll get if you're going to stand there all morning.' She goes to the yard wall and hauls the sluice. A mark of the basin comes off into the vats in a blue rush.".
    On discuss { Decrease level(dyers) by 1. Assert drawnToday(vat_yard). Assert toldDraw(vat_yard). Assert askedEarly(actor). }
  }
  Event mag_ruined near mag when vatsDrowned(vat_yard) "Mag Torrin stands in the grey water of her yard with the paddle still in her hand. She does not shout. She looks at you, a long time, as if to be sure of your face." then {
    Assert grievance(mag, party). }
  Relation grievance(group, group).
  Topic mag_after with mag "Say something to Mag Torrin about her vats" when vatsDrowned(vat_yard) once {
    Says "'Don't,' she says. 'You wanted the floor of my basin and you got it. I hope there was something on it worth a season.' She wades to the nearest vat and starts bailing it with her hands. Over her shoulder: 'I'll be at the Council. I'll say what you did. I'll say it in a good clear voice.'".
  }

  // Abel Lusk and the Lock-Rhyme.
  Observe lusk_scene at lusk_room when true "A kitchen with one chair by the stove and a lock-keeper's brass horn on a nail over it. On the shelf, a row of small clay figures of men and women each holding a lock-wheel: forty of them, the keepers he taught, he says, though he made them himself and some of them flatter.".
  Person abel "Abel Lusk" at lusk_room {
    Role "who kept the Ninth Lock for forty years". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. Manner cheerful.
  }
  Discovery lock_rhyme "The Lock-Rhyme, which every keeper learns: Upper to Dyer at the bell of six, / Dyer to vat when the third bell ticks; / Rise at the Sixth, and the Deep goes up, / Count at the Seventh, it takes its cup; / Grey from the Rim when the Mere is low, / And the high voice never, or down we go." { Known by abel. }
  Topic abel_rhyme with abel "Ask Abel Lusk for the Lock-Rhyme" when true once {
    Says "Abel sits up straight, puts his hands on his knees, and says it as a boy says it in school, in a sing-song, with a little bounce on the beat. 'Upper to Dyer at the bell of six, / Dyer to vat when the third bell ticks; / Rise at the Sixth, and the Deep goes up, / Count at the Seventh, it takes its cup; / Grey from the Rim when the Mere is low, / And the high voice never, or down we go.' He beams. 'Forty keepers. Every one of them could say that backwards drunk. The children in the Ward skip to it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lock_rhyme). }
  }
  Topic abel_deep with abel "Ask Abel what 'the Deep goes up' means" when knows(actor, lock_rhyme) once {
    Says "'The Deep Gate. Bottom of my old lock, a great bronze door in the floor.' He shows you with his hands, flat, then tipping up on edge. 'At the Sixth Remainder, of an evening, up it comes by itself; and at the Seventh down it goes, by itself, and lets through a cupful the night long. The keeper's to watch it, that's all, and write it in the book, and if it ever didn't, send to the Sounding.' He chuckles. 'It always did. Forty years. You could set your supper by it.'".
  }
  Topic abel_grey with abel "Ask Abel what 'grey from the Rim' means" when knows(actor, lock_rhyme) once {
    Says "'Ah, now.' He scratches his jaw. 'That one nobody knows. My master didn't know. There's a grey arch up at the head, bricked, and some say that's it, and some say it's just a thing to rhyme with low.' He leans in. 'I'll tell you what I think. I think the old ones had a back way to the Deep, for a dry year. To feed it from the top when the Mere couldn't. And somebody bricked it, because what kind of fool sends good river down a hole?'".
  }
  Topic abel_high with abel "Ask Abel what 'the high voice never' means" when knows(actor, lock_rhyme) once {
    Says "His face changes; he looks, for a moment, like the boy who first learned it, and was frightened by it. 'Never sing the high note into the water. That's all it means. Every keeper's told it his first night, by his master, at the lock, with the lantern out.' He laughs, uneasily. 'Superstition. Children's stuff. Only I never did. Did you ever meet a keeper that did? No. Nor me.'".
  }
  Topic abel_piet with abel "Ask Abel about the keeper of the Ninth Lock now" when true once {
    Says "'Piet Harl. My last. Good lad, too careful by half, which is the right half.' Abel's smile goes. 'He came up to me the first winter of the new Hymn and said, Master Lusk, the Deep didn't come down. I said, then send to the Sounding, like the rhyme says. He said he had. I said, then send again.' He looks at his hands. 'That was three years ago. I'm an old man, I forget things. I should have gone down there myself.'".
  }
  Topic abel_hymn with abel "Ask Abel what he thinks of the Short Hymn" when true once {
    Says "'It's lovely,' says Abel, surprising you. 'It is. I went the once. All those young ones, the place full like a fish-market. Sabeth Orr's a wonder.' He shrugs. 'But they've cut the Remainders, and the rhyme's built on the Remainders. Rise at the Sixth, count at the Seventh. There's no Seventh now. I said so to a young Cantor and he said the rhyme was only a rhyme.' He looks at the clay keepers on the shelf. 'Well. So it is.'".
  }
  Topic abel_fountains with abel "Ask Abel whether anything else changed when the Hymn was shortened" when true once {
    Says "Abel thinks about it seriously; he is a man who has been asked very few serious questions lately and is enjoying this one. 'The fountains,' he says. 'Now you ask. When I was a boy the fountains hummed of an evening, after the Seventh, at the Fifth. You'd put your hand on the square fountain and feel it go. We called it the Bowl purring.' He frowns. 'It stopped the same winter. I thought I'd gone a bit deaf. Everybody my age thought they'd gone a bit deaf.'".
  }
  Topic abel_arch with abel "Show Abel Lusk the rubbing of the Dyers' arch" when carries(actor, rubbing) once {
    Says "Abel holds the cloth to the window a long time. 'Four mouths. Shut, a bit, open, wide.' He traces the marks beside them. 'And the notes go up. The bottom note by the shut mouth.' He gives it back to you slowly. 'That's the Deep, isn't it. Low for little. That's the Seventh, all low; a cupful.' He sits down. 'Forty years, and I never once thought the notes meant anything. Take it to Sabeth Orr. She'll know the notes.'".
  }
}
